cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use KeenForge in academic work, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  KeenForge: a local-first, offline image annotation and model-training desktop
  tool
type: software
authors:
  - name: "KeenForgeAI"
    website: "https://github.com/KeenForgeAI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KeenForgeAI/KeenForge"
url: "https://github.com/KeenForgeAI/KeenForge"
abstract: >-
  KeenForge is a desktop application for building object-detection datasets and
  models without writing code. It combines dataset cleaning, a human-in-the-loop
  active-learning annotation loop, and local model training in a single offline
  tool: label a small seed set, the model trains in the background, pre-labels
  the next batch, and the expert corrects it. When the dataset is finished, the
  model is trained. All processing runs locally; images never leave the machine.
keywords:
  - annotation
  - image annotation
  - active learning
  - human-in-the-loop
  - object detection
  - YOLO
  - offline
  - no-code
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-20"
